IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), the Twelfth Schedule: the contents of the directors' statement required by s 201(16) (and s 8(7), another part's).
-- Each paragraph is a list of what the statement must say. The text has no verb in most of them ("1. A statement as to whether ...", "5. The particulars of shares issued ..."), so
-- each paragraph is read as: the directors' statement must contain what the paragraph lists.
-- Where a paragraph has a trigger ("Where any option has been granted ..."), two functions are given: the first says whether the paragraph asks for the particulars (the "must state" question),
-- the second says whether the statement has them (the "does state" question, NOTHING where the paragraph asks for nothing).
-- The directors' statement is the document of s 201(16) (sgc1-s201-statement.l4); its input `the statement contains the information set out in the Twelfth Schedule` is the AND of what is below.
-- The register of s 164 is a later wave's: whether a director is interested in shares or debentures according to that register is an input named for the fact.
-- The title, the cross-reference line "Sections 8(7) and 201(16)" and the running headings are not rules (NOTES.md, inert reason 1).

§ `Twelfth Schedule paragraph 1: the opinion of the directors`

-- src:28902 | 1. A statement as to whether in the opinion of the directors —
-- src:28904 | (a) the financial statements and, where applicable, the consolidated
-- src:28905 | financial statements are drawn up so as to give a true and fair view
-- src:28906 | of the financial position and performance of the company and
-- src:28913 | (if applicable) of the financial position and performance of the group
-- src:28914 | for the period covered by the financial statements or consolidated
-- src:28915 | financial statements; and
-- src:28917 | (b) at the date of the statement there are reasonable grounds to believe that
-- src:28918 | the company will be able to pay its debts as and when they fall due.
@ref sch 12 para 1 (src:28902-28918)
GIVEN `the statement says whether in the opinion of the directors the financial statements and, where applicable, the consolidated financial statements are drawn up so as to give a true and fair view of the financial position and performance of the company and, if applicable, of the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says whether in the opinion of the directors, at the date of the statement, there are reasonable grounds to believe that the company will be able to pay its debts as and when they fall due` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 1 the statement contains the matters the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF    `the statement says whether in the opinion of the directors the financial statements and, where applicable, the consolidated financial statements are drawn up so as to give a true and fair view of the financial position and performance of the company and, if applicable, of the group`
       AND `the statement says whether in the opinion of the directors, at the date of the statement, there are reasonable grounds to believe that the company will be able to pay its debts as and when they fall due`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A statement as to whether in the opinion of the directors — (a) the financial statements ... are drawn up so as to give a true and fair view ...; and (b) at the date of the statement there are reasonable grounds to believe that the company will be able to pay its debts as and when they fall due" (a duty not met: the provision's own question; the paragraph asks for a statement "as to whether", so a statement that gives the opinion either way meets it)

§ `Twelfth Schedule paragraph 2: options granted`

-- src:28920 | 2. Where any option has been granted by a company, other than a parent
-- src:28921 | company for which consolidated financial statements are required, during the
-- src:28922 | period covered by the financial statements to take up unissued shares of a
-- src:28923 | company —
-- src:28925 | (a) the number and class of shares in respect of which the option has been
-- src:28926 | granted;
-- src:28928 | (b) the date of expiration of the option;
-- src:28930 | (c) the basis upon which the option may be exercised; and
-- src:28932 | (d) whether the person to whom the option has been granted has any right
-- src:28933 | to participate by virtue of the option in any share issue of any other
-- src:28934 | company.
@ref sch 12 para 2 (src:28920-28934)
GIVEN `an option has been granted by the company during the period covered by the financial statements to take up unissued shares of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 2 the statement must state the particulars of the option` MEANS
    IF `an option has been granted by the company during the period covered by the financial statements to take up unissued shares of a company` AND (NOT `the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any option has been granted by a company, other than a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required, during the period covered by the financial statements to take up unissued shares of a company —" (a "where" condition: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); "other than a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required" is the "(other than X)" case, one of the six left to the encoder, put inside the same gate; the other reading is NOTHING)

@ref sch 12 para 2 (src:28920-28934)
GIVEN `an option has been granted by the company during the period covered by the financial statements to take up unissued shares of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the number and class of shares in respect of which the option has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the date of expiration of the option` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the basis upon which the option may be exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says whether the person to whom the option has been granted has any right to participate by virtue of the option in any share issue of any other company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 2 the statement states the particulars of the option` MEANS
    IF `sch 12 para 2 the statement must state the particulars of the option` `an option has been granted by the company during the period covered by the financial statements to take up unissued shares of a company` `the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF    `the statement gives the number and class of shares in respect of which the option has been granted`
             AND `the statement gives the date of expiration of the option`
             AND `the statement gives the basis upon which the option may be exercised`
             AND `the statement says whether the person to whom the option has been granted has any right to participate by virtue of the option in any share issue of any other company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the number and class of shares in respect of which the option has been granted; (b) the date of expiration of the option; (c) the basis upon which the option may be exercised; and (d) whether the person to whom the option has been granted has any right to participate" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph asks for particulars of an option granted in the period by a company other than a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required, and says nothing about the statement of any other company

§ `Twelfth Schedule paragraph 3: particulars already stated`

-- src:28936 | 3. Where any of the particulars required by paragraph 2 have been stated in a
-- src:28937 | previous directors’ statement, or a previous directors’ report that was made for the
-- src:28938 | purposes of section 201(5) or (6A) as in force immediately before 1 July 2015,
-- src:28939 | they may be stated by reference to that statement or report.
@ref sch 12 para 3 (src:28936-28939)
GIVEN `the particulars required by paragraph 2 have been stated in a previous directors' statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars required by paragraph 2 have been stated in a previous directors' report made for the purposes of section 201(5) or (6A) as in force immediately before 1 July 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 3 the particulars may be stated by reference to the earlier statement or report` MEANS
    IF    `the particulars required by paragraph 2 have been stated in a previous directors' statement`
       OR `the particulars required by paragraph 2 have been stated in a previous directors' report made for the purposes of section 201(5) or (6A) as in force immediately before 1 July 2015`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any of the particulars required by paragraph 2 have been stated in a previous directors' statement, or a previous directors' report ..., they may be stated by reference to that statement or report" (a "may" gated by "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 3, says do not change it and list it for the maintainer; fork F-sch12-3, NOTES.md)

§ `Twelfth Schedule paragraph 4: options in a parent company's group`

-- src:28943 | 4. Where a parent company or any of its subsidiary corporations has at any time
-- src:28944 | granted to a person an option to have shares issued to the person in the company or
-- src:28945 | subsidiary corporation, the directors’ statement of the parent company must state
-- src:28946 | the name of the corporation in respect of the shares in which the option was
-- src:28947 | granted and the other particulars required under paragraphs 2, 5 and 6.
@ref sch 12 para 4 (src:28943-28947)
GIVEN `the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parent company or any of its subsidiary corporations has at any time granted to a person an option to have shares issued to the person in the company or subsidiary corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 4 the directors' statement of the parent company must state the corporation and the other particulars` MEANS
    IF `the company is a parent company` AND `the parent company or any of its subsidiary corporations has at any time granted to a person an option to have shares issued to the person in the company or subsidiary corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a parent company or any of its subsidiary corporations has at any time granted to a person an option ..., the directors' statement of the parent company must state" (a duty gated by "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); the duty's own question, the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2)

@ref sch 12 para 4 (src:28943-28947)
GIVEN `the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parent company or any of its subsidiary corporations has at any time granted to a person an option to have shares issued to the person in the company or subsidiary corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the name of the corporation in respect of the shares in which the option was granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the other particulars required under paragraphs 2, 5 and 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 4 the statement states the corporation and the other particulars` MEANS
    IF `sch 12 para 4 the directors' statement of the parent company must state the corporation and the other particulars` `the company is a parent company` `the parent company or any of its subsidiary corporations has at any time granted to a person an option to have shares issued to the person in the company or subsidiary corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF `the statement gives the name of the corporation in respect of the shares in which the option was granted` AND `the statement gives the other particulars required under paragraphs 2, 5 and 6`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must state the name of the corporation in respect of the shares in which the option was granted and the other particulars required under paragraphs 2, 5 and 6" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of the directors' statement of a parent company where it or a subsidiary corporation has granted an option, and says nothing about any other statement

§ `Twelfth Schedule paragraph 5: shares issued on the exercise of options`

-- src:28949 | 5. The particulars of shares issued during the period to which the statement
-- src:28950 | relates by virtue of the exercise of options to take up unissued shares of the
-- src:28951 | company, whether granted before or during that period.
@ref sch 12 para 5 (src:28949-28951)
GIVEN `shares were issued during the period to which the statement relates by virtue of the exercise of options to take up unissued shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the particulars of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 5 the statement states the particulars of shares issued on the exercise of options` MEANS
    IF NOT `shares were issued during the period to which the statement relates by virtue of the exercise of options to take up unissued shares of the company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph asks for "the particulars of shares issued during the period ... by virtue of the exercise of options", and says nothing where no such shares were issued (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE IF `the statement gives the particulars of those shares`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The particulars of shares issued during the period to which the statement relates by virtue of the exercise of options to take up unissued shares of the company, whether granted before or during that period" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

§ `Twelfth Schedule paragraph 6: unissued shares under option`

-- src:28953 | 6. The number and class of unissued shares of the company under option as at
-- src:28954 | the end of the period to which the statement relates, the price, or method of fixing
-- src:28955 | the price, of issue of those shares, the date of expiration of the option and the rights
-- src:28956 | (if any) of the persons to whom the options have been granted to participate by
-- src:28957 | virtue of the options in any share issue of any other company.
@ref sch 12 para 6 (src:28953-28957)
GIVEN `there are unissued shares of the company under option as at the end of the period to which the statement relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the number and class of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the price, or method of fixing the price, of issue of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the date of expiration of the option` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the rights, if any, of the persons to whom the options have been granted to participate by virtue of the options in any share issue of any other company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 6 the statement states the unissued shares under option` MEANS
    IF NOT `there are unissued shares of the company under option as at the end of the period to which the statement relates`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph asks for "the number and class of unissued shares of the company under option as at the end of the period", and says nothing where there are none (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE IF    `the statement gives the number and class of those shares`
            AND `the statement gives the price, or method of fixing the price, of issue of those shares`
            AND `the statement gives the date of expiration of the option`
            AND `the statement gives the rights, if any, of the persons to whom the options have been granted to participate by virtue of the options in any share issue of any other company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The number and class of unissued shares of the company under option as at the end of the period ..., the price, or method of fixing the price, of issue of those shares, the date of expiration of the option and the rights (if any) of the persons to whom the options have been granted" (a duty not met: the provision's own question; "(if any)" asks for the rights where there are some, and a statement that gives none where none exist is read as meeting it, NOTES.md)

§ `Twelfth Schedule paragraph 7: the directors in office`

-- src:28959 | 7. The names of the persons who are the directors in office at the date of the
-- src:28960 | statement.
@ref sch 12 para 7 (src:28959-28960)
GIVEN `the statement gives the names of the persons who are the directors in office at the date of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 7 the statement states the names of the directors in office` MEANS
    IF `the statement gives the names of the persons who are the directors in office at the date of the statement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The names of the persons who are the directors in office at the date of the statement" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

§ `Twelfth Schedule paragraph 8: arrangements to enable directors to acquire shares or debentures`

-- src:28967 | 8. Whether at the end of the financial year to which the financial statements or,
-- src:28968 | where the company is a parent company, consolidated financial statements
-- src:28969 | relate —
-- src:28971 | (a) there subsist arrangements to which the company is a party, being
-- src:28972 | arrangements whose objects are, or one of whose objects is, to enable
-- src:28973 | directors of the company to acquire benefits by means of the
-- src:28974 | acquisition of shares in, or debentures of, the company or any other
-- src:28975 | body corporate; or
-- src:28977 | (b) there have, at any time in that year, subsisted such arrangements as
-- src:28978 | aforesaid to which the company was a party,
-- src:28980 | and if so, a statement explaining the effect of the arrangements and giving the
-- src:28981 | names of the persons who at any time in that year were directors of the company
-- src:28982 | and held, or whose nominees held, shares or debentures acquired pursuant to the
-- src:28983 | arrangements.
@ref sch 12 para 8 (src:28967-28983)
GIVEN `arrangements of the kind the paragraph describes subsisted at the end of the financial year or at any time in that year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 8 the statement must also explain the effect of the arrangements and name the directors` MEANS
    IF `arrangements of the kind the paragraph describes subsisted at the end of the financial year or at any time in that year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and if so, a statement explaining the effect of the arrangements and giving the names of the persons who at any time in that year were directors of the company and held ... shares or debentures acquired pursuant to the arrangements" (a duty gated by "if so": the duty's own question, the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2)

@ref sch 12 para 8 (src:28967-28983)
GIVEN `the statement says whether arrangements of the kind the paragraph describes subsisted at the end of the financial year or at any time in that year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `arrangements of the kind the paragraph describes subsisted at the end of the financial year or at any time in that year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement explains the effect of the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the names of the persons who at any time in that year were directors of the company and held, or whose nominees held, shares or debentures acquired pursuant to the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 8 the statement states whether the arrangements subsisted and, if so, their effect` MEANS
    IF NOT `the statement says whether arrangements of the kind the paragraph describes subsisted at the end of the financial year or at any time in that year`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "8. Whether at the end of the financial year ... (a) there subsist arrangements ...; or (b) there have, at any time in that year, subsisted such arrangements" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)
    ELSE IF NOT `arrangements of the kind the paragraph describes subsisted at the end of the financial year or at any time in that year`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE (IF `the statement explains the effect of the arrangements` AND `the statement gives the names of the persons who at any time in that year were directors of the company and held, or whose nominees held, shares or debentures acquired pursuant to the arrangements`
               THEN JUST TRUE
               ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and if so, a statement explaining the effect of the arrangements and giving the names of the persons who ..." (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

§ `Twelfth Schedule paragraph 9: the directors' interests in shares and debentures`

-- src:28985 | 9. As respects each person who, at the end of the financial year, was a director of
-- src:28986 | the company —
-- src:28988 | (a) whether or not (according to the register kept by the company for the
-- src:28989 | purposes of section 164 relating to the obligation of a director of a
-- src:28990 | company to notify it of his or her interests in shares in, or debentures
-- src:28991 | of, the company and of every other body corporate, being the
-- src:28992 | company’s subsidiary or holding company or a subsidiary of the
-- src:28993 | company’s holding company) he or she was, at the end of that year,
-- src:28994 | interested in shares in, or debentures of, the company or any other such
-- src:28995 | body corporate; and
-- src:28997 | (b) if he or she was, the number and amount of shares in, and debentures
-- src:28998 | of, each body (specifying it) in which, according to that register, he or
-- src:28999 | she was then interested and whether or not, according to that register,
-- src:29000 | he or she was, at the beginning of that year (or, if he or she was not then
-- src:29001 | a director, when he or she became a director), interested in shares in, or
-- src:29002 | debentures of, the company or any other such body corporate and, if he
-- src:29003 | or she was, the number and amount of shares in, and debentures of,
-- src:29004 | each body (specifying it) in which, according to that register, he or she
-- src:29005 | was interested at the beginning of that year or (as the case may be)
-- src:29006 | when he or she became a director.
@ref sch 12 para 9 (src:28985-29006)
GIVEN `the person was a director of the company at the end of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says whether or not, according to the register kept for the purposes of section 164, the director was at the end of that year interested in shares in, or debentures of, the company or any other such body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `according to that register the director was at the end of that year interested in shares in, or debentures of, the company or any other such body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the number and amount of shares in, and debentures of, each body, specifying it, in which according to that register the director was then interested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says whether or not, according to that register, the director was at the beginning of that year, or when the director became a director, interested in shares in, or debentures of, the company or any other such body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `according to that register the director was at the beginning of that year, or when the director became a director, interested in shares in, or debentures of, the company or any other such body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the number and amount of shares in, and debentures of, each body, specifying it, in which according to that register the director was interested at the beginning of that year or when the director became a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 9 the statement states the director's interests in shares and debentures` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person was a director of the company at the end of the financial year`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "each person who, at the end of the financial year, was a director of the company", and says nothing of anyone else (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE IF NOT `the statement says whether or not, according to the register kept for the purposes of section 164, the director was at the end of that year interested in shares in, or debentures of, the company or any other such body corporate`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) whether or not (according to the register kept by the company for the purposes of section 164 ...) he or she was, at the end of that year, interested in shares in, or debentures of, the company or any other such body corporate" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)
         ELSE IF NOT `according to that register the director was at the end of that year interested in shares in, or debentures of, the company or any other such body corporate`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE IF NOT (`the statement gives the number and amount of shares in, and debentures of, each body, specifying it, in which according to that register the director was then interested` AND `the statement says whether or not, according to that register, the director was at the beginning of that year, or when the director became a director, interested in shares in, or debentures of, the company or any other such body corporate`)
                   THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if he or she was, the number and amount of shares in, and debentures of, each body (specifying it) in which, according to that register, he or she was then interested and whether or not, according to that register, he or she was, at the beginning of that year ... interested" (a duty gated by "if he or she was": the duty's own question)
                   ELSE IF NOT `according to that register the director was at the beginning of that year, or when the director became a director, interested in shares in, or debentures of, the company or any other such body corporate`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE (IF `the statement gives the number and amount of shares in, and debentures of, each body, specifying it, in which according to that register the director was interested at the beginning of that year or when the director became a director`
                              THEN JUST TRUE
                              ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and, if he or she was, the number and amount of shares in, and debentures of, each body (specifying it) in which, according to that register, he or she was interested at the beginning of that year or (as the case may be) when he or she became a director" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)
